vo_avfoundation: let OSD changes wait as bitmap lists

A subtitle change was drawn and enqueued with its frame's video sample,
queue-lead-ms (128) ahead: at 24 fps the OSD layer's queue holds 2.5-3
canvases for later frames, 13.8 MB each on a 2736x1260 layer and 33 MB on a
3840x2160 one. Of the 5 canvases alive on a typeset track those are half.

--avfoundation-osd-queue-lead-ms=<ms> (default 0: as before) keeps a
change as its frame's bitmap list (the items and a reference on their
atlas) and draws and enqueues it only at the last flip that still leaves
that lead before its frame: when waiting for the next flip, one frame
spacing later, would leave less (avf_osd_change_due). A pause sends
whatever waits; a seek, a canvas change and an option change drop it with
the rest of the OSD state; if no flip comes (the last frames of a file) a
timer, pushed on by every flip, looks again a frame spacing later. Off by
default because it trades margin for memory: a VO thread stalled for longer
than the lead shows that change late, which a 128 ms queue hides.

iPhone Air, 40 ms, interleaved with 0048 alone, n = 3 (taken while 0048
still cleared a buffer of unknown contents band by band, hence its 9.63 and
12.67 %; not repeated since): anime-ass.mkv footprint 201 / 207 MB (mean /
peak) -> 188 / 198 MB and 9.63 -> 9.11 % of a core; a real opening 312 /
370 -> 296 / 356 MB, 12.67 -> 12.28 %; no dropped frame. In step with the
video: screenshots of a file that carries its frame number in the picture
and in the subtitles show the same number in 83 of 83 shots (82 of 82
without the option, 83 of 83 unpatched); a prototype with 20, 40 and 60 ms:
74 of 74, 73 of 73, 75 of 75. With the VO thread held once a second (one
launch per cell): held 60 ms, 78 of 79 shots in step and one a frame late
with 40 ms, 81 of 81 without the option; held 100 ms, 75 of 79 with 40 ms
(three a frame late, one two), 67 of 75 with 80 ms, 75 of 77 without. Not
measured at 60 fps. Pause, exact and keyframe seeks, a seek while paused,
the end of the file with keep-open and loadfile replace behave and time as
before (n = 2). scripts/test_avf_osd_ahead.sh covers when a change is due.

